-- title:
--   Regular special fibre on the pole chart, q = 3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 3$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K \subseteq L((t))$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero whose image in $L((t))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, and form the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closure `chartAlgInf` of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, together with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((t))$ after pushing coefficients to $L$. Let $z \in \mathfrak{X}$, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ pulled back from $\varpi$ along `toBase`, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Assume $z$ is the image under the pole-chart immersion of a point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf A K j` whose prime ideal is maximal and contains every element of `chartAlgInf A K j` that is a non-unit of $W_0$. Let $K_0 \subseteq K$ be the field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, made an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j_0 \in K_0$ be non-zero with the same $q$-expansion as $j$; let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from `chartAlgInf A K₀ j₀` to `chartAlgInf A K j` compatible with the inclusion $K_0 \subseteq K$, and assume the structure morphism `toBase` of the two-chart model of $K_0$ over $A$ is smooth. Then, with `chartAlgInf A K j` regarded as an algebra over `chartAlgInf A K₀ j₀` via $\iota$: if this algebra is unramified at every height-one prime $\mathfrak{Q}$ of `chartAlgInf A K j` contained in the prime of $y$, then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is a purity-of-the-branch-locus statement for the Igusa-level two-chart model: smoothness of the level-$M'$ floor over $A$ together with unramifiedness in codimension one propagates to regularity of the special fibre of the upper model at a closed point of the pole chart lying on the branch cut out by the non-units of the Gauss valuation ring. It is the $q = 3$ case, companion to the case $q \ge 5$, and feeds the analysis of the special fibre at primes of the pole chart carried out in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_not_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_not_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_three).
